  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "A prism is a transparent optical object, usually made of glass or plastic,
    with flat polished surfaces. When light enters a prism, its direction changes
    because light travels at different speeds in air and glass. This bending of light
    is called refraction.\n\nWhen white light passes through a triangular prism,
    it separates into different colours. This process is called dispersion of light.
    The seven visible colours are Violet, Indigo, Blue, Green, Yellow, Orange, and
    Red (VIBGYOR).\n\nEach colour bends by a slightly different amount because each
    has a different wavelength. Violet light bends the most, while red light bends
    the least. This causes the colours to spread out and form a visible spectrum.\n\nPrisms
    are commonly used in optical experiments, spectrometers, binoculars, cameras,
    and other scientific instruments to study and control light.\n\nKey takeaway:\nWhite
    light + Prism \u2192 Refraction + Dispersion \u2192 Seven-colour spectrum"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
